+/* This section of implementation is to remove the 32ILP-ABI overhead where
+   unnecessary zero-extension instructions are introduced. The criteria of
+   the optimization is that a pointer has to be zero-extended after it is
+   loaded from memory. Otherwise, the register which stores the pointer value
+   is considered as partial dirty. An zero-extension instruction following an 
+   pointer arithmetic instruction is redundant if the source operand of 
+   the extension instruction is not partial dirty.
+
+   Where to put this target dependent code ?
+*/
