+compile it with @option{-fsection-anchors}, it will access the variables
+from a common anchor point instead.  The effect is similar to the
+following pseudocode (which isn't valid C):
+
+@smallexample
+int foo (void)
+@{
+  register int *xr = &x;
+  return xr[&a - &x] + xr[&b - &x] + xr[&c - &x];
+@}
+@end smallexample
+
